  "chitchat": [
    "Wendel turns a bolt over, finds the thread he wants, and drops it into a paper bag without looking.",
    "\"If it moves and it shouldn't, tape. If it should move and it doesn't, oil. That's the whole trade.\"",
    "Somewhere in the back, something is cut, and the smell of hot steel drifts through."
  ],
  "description": "A wide, unhurried man in a canvas apron with a pencil behind each ear, one for wood and one for metal, and he will tell you which is which if you ask. He has never once said a thing couldn't be fixed. He has, several times, said it wasn't worth fixing, which he considers a completely different sentence.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Mind the stock under the awning. It bites at the ankle.\""
    },
    "chalk": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "He doesn't turn round. \"Fella says a thing's fixed when it works. I say a thing's fixed when it works without you.\" A long pause. \"He's been winning for about a year, which tells you something about the year.\""
    },
    "fix": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Show me, then.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"I sell parts. Watts up at the turbine hall does benches.\" He taps a drawer. \"What I'll do is tell you which of these you actually need, which is usually the cheaper one, and that's why I'm still here and the place before me isn't.\""
    },
    "gossip": {
      "actions": [
        {
          "action": "GOSSIP_TELL"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"People tell you things while you're counting screws. I don't think they notice they're doing it.\""
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Let's see the pegboard.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Can you fix things, or just sell parts?",
          "next": "fix"
        },
        {
          "label": "What's the chalk argument on the back wall?",
          "next": "chalk"
        },
        {
          "label": "Heard anything worth hearing?",
          "next": "gossip"
        },
        {
          "label": "Nothing today.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Wendel looks you over the way he'd look over a bracket. \"Right. What's broken, or what are you about to break?\" He sets down a pencil. \"Either's fine. I stock for both.\""
    }
  },
